Insertion at the Head of a Linked List

Problem: Given the head of a singly linked list and an integer "X", insert a new node with value "X" at the beginning (head) of the linked list and return the head of the modified linked list.

Approach:

- Create a new node with the given value "X".
- Set the next reference of the new node to the current head ("newNode.next = head").
- Update the head to point to the newly created node ("head = newNode").
- The new node becomes the first node of the linked list.
- Return the updated head.
- If the linked list is empty, the new node becomes the only node.

Time Complexity: O(1) – A new node is created and inserted at the beginning without traversing the linked list.

Space Complexity: O(1) – Only one new node is created.

Concepts Used:

- Singly Linked List
- Node Insertion
- Head Pointer
- New Node Creation
- Reference Manipulation
- Node Linking

###Solution

class Solution {
    public ListNode insertAtHead(ListNode head, int X) {
        return new ListNode(X, head);
    }
}
